From: ACK72 <ACK72@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:35:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] clk: en7523: initialize the PERSTOUT reset value

Both branches OR into an uninitialized local, so the asserted value
depends on stack contents: a stray bit in the register window makes
en7523_reset_update() write the opposite polarity for the dedicated
PERSTOUT resets. Assign the masked value directly.

Signed-off-by: ACK72 <ACK72@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
@@ -1068,9 +1068,9 @@
 
 	/* For PCIC reset logic is inverted, 0:assert 1:deassert*/
 	if (addr == REG_NP_SCU_PCIC)
-		val |= assert ? 0 : BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK);
+		val = assert ? 0 : BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK);
 	else
-		val |= assert ? BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK) : 0;
+		val = assert ? BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK) : 0;
 
 	regmap_update_bits(rst_data->map, addr, BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK),
 			   val);
